What is Factory Design Pattern ?

Factory Design Pattern is a creational design pattern. It is Used when we want to create an object, but
we dont want the code that uses those objects to worry about how object is created.

Factory Design pattern is used to only about creation of Object.

Instead for creating the object using new keyword ask the Factory to create the object for You.


For Example :

interface Pizza{
    int getCost();
}

class PaneerPizza implements Pizza{
    int getCost(){
     return 200;
    }
}

class VeggiesPizza implements Pizza{
     int getCost(){
      return 150;
     }
}

class PizzaFactory{
    public static Pizza getPizza(String type){
         if(type.equals("Veggies")){
            return new VeggiesPizza();
         }
         else if(type.equals("Paneer")){
            return new PaneerPizza();
         }
         else{ throw exception };
    }
}

class Main{
    public static void main(String args[]){
        Pizza pizza = PizzaFactory.getPizza("Paneer");
        int cost = pizza.getCost();
    }
}